{#-
  Notice under each video facade, shown before the visitor presses play
  (SPEC §9.1, §15.1). It makes pressing play an informed choice about
  YouTube's storage. Draft wording until HREC approval.

  A macro (not a plain include), so the id is passed in rather than read
  from whatever is in scope:
    {% from "notices/video.njk" import videoNotice %}
    {{ videoNotice('video-notice-' + video.video_id) }}
  partials/video.njk calls it for every facade; templates don't need to.

  `id` goes on the notice's two sentences (not its link). The play control
  names it in aria-describedby, so a screen reader hears the notice with
  "Play video" although the notice comes after it in the page.

  The notice doesn't link the handout: the row of controls under it
  (partials/video-controls.njk) has the video's "Handout" button, its text
  alternative (SPEC §9.3), and a second link would only repeat it.
-#}
{%- macro videoNotice(id='') -%}
<p class="notice-text video__notice"><span{% if id %} id="{{ id }}"{% endif %}>Pressing play loads this video from YouTube (Google). YouTube may then store cookies in your browser and collect information about what you watch.</span> <a href="/privacy/#cookies-and-browser-storage">More about this</a></p>
{%- endmacro -%}
